{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nosophobic-mammoth-wrenchbird","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Decompose PydanticAIRunner.run() and stop the recurrence\n\nImplements ADR 0055 (docs/adr/0055-runner-decomposition-and-per-function-size-gate.md). Read it\nfirst; every decision and every rejected alternative is recorded there with measured evidence.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nrunner.py has been split THREE times (c1f4 -146, task 2682 -152, task 3a98 -35) and is at 689 lines,\n782 with task cc33 pending against an 800 hard cap. Ticket 1484 relieved the identical pressure in\ngate_dispatch.py and orchestrator.py weeks earlier.\n\nMEASURED at 97791145f: PydanticAIRunner.run() spans 219-626 = 408 lines, 59% of the file (227 code,\n166 comment, 15 blank). Every prior split extracted a CALLEE, which always satisfies a per-FILE gate\nwhile leaving the calling method untouched -- so the method keeps absorbing work and the file\nregrows. We split the nouns while the pressure sat on the verb.\n\nA VERIFIED latent defect makes this urgent rather than cosmetic: ProviderSession(cfg) is constructed\nat runner.py:301 but the try guarding it starts at 474 and its finally-close at 582. Lines 301-473\nare OUTSIDE the guard and several raise by design, leaking an opened httpx.AsyncClient.\nProviderSession.__enter__/__exit__ exist (providers.py:295-299) and are NEVER used -- while\nproviders.py:21 documents \"runner.run() wraps its body in `with ProviderSession(cfg) as session:`\".\nThe docstring describes a caller that does not exist.\n\n## Approach\n\nPer ADR 0055: a per-function RATCHET gate (the durable half), the session-guard correctness fix, and\nextraction of PLAIN FUNCTIONS with explicit parameters -- explicitly NOT the frozen carrier object an\nearlier draft proposed, which an adversarial review showed would be decorative (two of its seven\nfields are mutated after construction, and cc33 writes provenance AFTER the finally block).\n\n## Scope\n\nChildren deliver it. This parent owns only the sequencing and the end-state assertion.\n\n## Sequencing constraint\n\nLAND NOTHING HERE UNTIL task cc33 MERGES. cc33 adds ~97 lines to runner.py at seven distinct sites,\nfour of which these children move. Rebasing this work onto cc33 is a different diff than authoring it\nagainst 97791145f.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] every child ticket is closed\n- [ ] runner.py is under 500 LOC and PydanticAIRunner.run() is under 120 lines, both MEASURED in the\n      close comment (ADR 0055 projects ~380 and 60-90; the criterion is the looser bound so a\n      reasonable outcome is not blocked by an estimate)\n- [ ] the per-function ratchet gate is green in CI at a value at or below 120\n- [ ] the full suite passes with no test ASSERTION changed; every monkeypatch repoint is listed in\n      its own commit message with the name and the reason\n","id":"7f86-d935-3742-476a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Decompose PydanticAIRunner.run() and add a per-function size ratchet"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785510574488361001,"uuid":"2067e650-754c-4b07-ab40-266c47db4bb3"}